---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"leds\", \"set\"])"
---
Change the LEDs live, with no reboot (needs control channel v1.1 of the gamepadii firmware, or v1.2 on main). RAM only unless --save: the pad goes back to its saved LED settings when it restarts

Usage: gamepadii leds set [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --animation <NAME|N>
          The animation: static-color, rainbow, chase, static-theme, custom-theme, or its number

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --brightness <N|up|down>
          The brightness level (0 to the pad's steps), up or down

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --static-color <NAME|N>
          The static-color animation's colour: black, white, red, orange, yellow, limegreen, green, seafoam, aqua, skyblue, blue, purple, pink, magenta, indigo, violet, or its number

      --button-color <NAME|N>
          The colour of a pressed button (same names)

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --theme <NAME|N>
          The static-theme animation's theme: static-rainbow, xbox, playstation, neogeo, street-fighter-2, tekken, ..., or its number

      --lights-profile <N|off>
          Main firmware: the lights profile, from 0, or off. The other options above, except --brightness, are for the v0.7.12 line

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

      --save
          Also save it to flash, as the LED hotkeys do (alone: save what runs now). In PS4/PS5 mode the firmware skips saves while the controller authentication needs the flash

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
